# Schema follow-ups

- Reduce WASM size by using one TOML reader and replacing the `yaml_rust2` structural event scan. Changing TOML readers changes fixture error text; `wasm-opt` would add a Binaryen build dependency.
- Preserve integer-like mapping key order across the JavaScript boundary with a pairs array; this changes the JS contract.
- Preserve upgrade diagnostics as warnings on installed readings. A pre-v1 spelling can trigger an upgrade that sets aside an invalid value without reporting it.
- Count bracket depth outside quoted scalars in `src/frontmatter.rs`; raw bracket counting can reject a valid quoted string.
- Reject NUL path components in `FileTree::insert` if a caller stores paths where NUL matters.
